Why This Is Asked

Tests practical ability to design a scalable, tenant-aware data intake: dynamic schemas, low-latency validation, and reliable processing.

Key Concepts

- Event-driven ingestion with per-tenant schema discovery
- Caching and TTL for schema lookups
- Fast validation library (e.g., Ajv)
- Idempotent writes and deduplication
- Dead-letter queue for bad data
- Schema evolution testing and compatibility checks

Code Example

```javascript
// Ingestion function (Node.js)
const ajv = new Ajv();
let schemaCache = new Map();
async function getSchemaForTenant(tenantId){
  if(schemaCache.has(tenantId)) return schemaCache.get(tenantId);
  const cfg = await AppConfigClient.getConfigurationSetting({key: `schema:${tenantId}`});
  const schema = JSON.parse(cfg.value);
  schemaCache.set(tenantId, schema);
  setTimeout(() => schemaCache.delete(tenantId), 60_000);
  return schema;
}
async function validateAndRoute(msg){
  const tenantId = msg.tenantId;
  const schema = await getSchemaForTenant(tenantId);
  const validate = ajv.compile(schema);
  const valid = validate(msg.payload);
  if(!valid){ await DLQ.push({tenantId, msg, errors: validate.errors}); return; }
  await CosmosDB.upsert('events', tenantId, msg.payload, {dedupId: msg.id});
}
```

Follow-up Questions

- How would you test schema evolution across tenants and ensure backward compatibility?
- How would you handle schema removal or deprecation without breaking in-flight events?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluate ability to implement observability across heterogeneous runtimes in Azure, with end-to-end tracing and cross-service propagation.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry across Functions, AKS, Databricks
- W3C TraceContext; OTLP exporting to Azure Monitor
- Context propagation through queues and Delta Lake
- Sampling strategies and trace retention

## Code Example
```javascript
const { trace, context, propagation } = require('@opentelemetry/api');
const { NodeTracerProvider } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-node');
const { SimpleSpanProcessor } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-base');
const { OTLPTraceExporter } = require('@opentelemetry/exporter-otlp-http');

const provider = new NodeTracerProvider();
const exporter = new OTLPTraceExporter({ url: 'https://<region>.monitor.azure.com/v1/traces' });
provider.addSpanProcessor(new SimpleSpanProcessor(exporter));
provider.register();

module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tracer = trace.getTracer('example-function');
  const span = tracer.startSpan('http-request');
  // downstream calls propagate context automatically when using OpenTelemetry API
  span.end();
  return { status: 200, body: 'OK' };
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test end-to-end traces across services?
- How would you adjust sampling in production without outages?

